I open the boxes and start to unpack.
I hang the clothes in the closet.
My shirts lie on the shelf.
The shoes stand by the door.
Then I make the bed.
I have a sheet, a warm blanket, and a soft pillow.
Now it all lies on the bed.
There is an empty box standing under the bed.
I sit down on the bed for a moment.
I look around in my new bedroom.
It is nice and quiet here.
Everything is in place now.
There are no more clothes lying in the boxes.
The room is small, but it is cozy.
It is starting to feel like my own.
I sit and relax.
